<section class="stride" id="stride" data-scene="ring">
  <div class="stride-head">
    <p class="section-label">(03) Threat model</p>
    <h2 data-split>Six ways<br />trust <em>breaks.</em></h2>
    <p class="stride-intro" data-fade>
      Every review checks all six STRIDE categories, and each project keeps a threat model the
      next review builds on.
    </p>
  </div>
  <ul class="stride-list" data-stride>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">S</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Spoofing</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Posing as a user, a service or a model you trust.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">T</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Tampering</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Changing data, prompts or files along the way.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">R</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Repudiation</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Actions that leave no trace of who asked for them.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">I</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Information disclosure</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Secrets, records or source landing in the wrong hands.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">D</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Denial of service</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Unbounded work, loops or spend that one request can set off.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stride-item" data-stride-item>
      <span class="stride-letter">E</span>
      <span class="stride-name">Elevation of privilege</span>
      <span class="stride-desc">Input or model output reaching a tool it never should.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
